# boss_design.md

This public-facing summary outlines the boss design goals while masking confidential encounter scripts and tuning data.

## Core Concepts
- Boss encounters remain major narrative and gameplay milestones that react to alignment and player choices.
- [REDACTED] replaces the specific scenario triggers, resistance tables, and dialogue sequencing logic.

## Boss Categories
- Faith-aligned, Veil-aligned, and neutral archetypes persist conceptually, but phase logic, counterplay scripts, and stat curves are `[REDACTED]`.
- Multi-phase encounters are supported through the boss management pipeline without revealing phase-by-phase tactics.

## Behavior Highlights (Sanitized)
- Boss behavior adapts to alignment and environmental states using internal hooks preserved from the original implementation.
- `[REDACTED]` conceals the concrete ability lists, passive modifiers, and reactive thresholds.

## Implementation Notes
- `BossManager` continues to orchestrate spawning, defeat notifications, and dialogue events.
- Alignment-driven stat adjustments and progression unlocks operate as described, with sensitive balancing data redacted in the archival backup.
